{% layout "layout.liquid" %}

{% block title %}About | CBT Workbook{% endblock %}

{% block main %}
<main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto p-6">
  <section class="text-center mb-8">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold gradient-text mb-4">What is this platform?</h1>
    <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">This is a self-guided mental wellness platform rooted in the principles of Cognitive Behavioral Therapy (CBT). It offers thoughtfully designed tools to help individuals understand their emotions, shift unhelpful thought patterns, and engage in meaningful actions — all in one supportive and structured digital space.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold text-purple-400 mb-4">Why CBT?</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">CBT is one of the most effective, evidence-based approaches for managing anxiety, depression, and everyday emotional struggles. By translating these therapeutic strategies into interactive tools, the platform makes mental health support accessible, practical, and easy to integrate into daily life.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold text-purple-400 mb-4">Features</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-300">
      <li class="mb-2">
        <strong class="text-white">Mood Tracker:</strong> Capture how you’re feeling in the moment. This tool allows you to log your emotional state, choosing from various options and intensity, alongside notes and context. Over time, users can observe emotional trends, spot triggers, and develop greater emotional self-awareness.
      </li>
      <li class="mb-2">
        <strong class="text-white">Thought Record Worksheet:</strong> Interrupt negative spirals through reflection. Based on classic CBT structure, this worksheet guides users through a 9-step process to analyze distressing thoughts. It helps separate fact from feeling, identify cognitive distortions (like catastrophizing or mind reading), and develop a more balanced, compassionate alternative thought.
      </li>
      <li class="mb-2">
        <strong class="text-white">Gratitude Journal:</strong> Reflect on and record things you are grateful for. This tool fosters a positive mindset and helps users focus on the good in their lives.
      </li>
      <li class="mb-2">
        <strong class="text-white">BDI (Beck Depression Inventory):</strong> A tool to assess and track depression levels, providing insights into mental health over time.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold text-purple-400 mb-4">Inspired by Feeling Good by Dr. David D. Burns</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">This project draws inspiration from the groundbreaking work of Dr. David D. Burns, psychiatrist and author of the best-selling book <em>Feeling Good: The New Mood Therapy</em>. His book brought CBT to the mainstream, empowering people to change how they feel by changing how they think.</p>
    <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">We’ve transformed many of the book’s core exercises into interactive, web-based tools — making them more accessible and easier to practice regularly.</p>
  </section>
</main>
{% endblock %}
